ent. Actually, hmm, \"AquaMaster4\" appears as part of the model. I'll set family_name to null to be safe.\n\nmatrix_tables entries:\n\nTable 9:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Table 9 — General characteristics of the indicating device (Reduced bore, AC mains powered)\",\n  \"columns\": [\"meter_size\", \"indicating_range_maximum\", \"indicating_range_minimum\", \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, \"m³\", \"m³\", \"m³\"],\n  \"description\": \"Indicating device characteristics for reduced bore meters powered from AC mains.\",\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN40, DN50, DN65\", \"indicating_range_maximum\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_minimum\": 99999, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": 0.0001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN80\", \"indicating_range_maximum\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_minimum\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": 0.0001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN100, DN125, DN150, DN200\", \"indicating_range_maximum\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_minimum\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": 0.001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN250\", \"indicating_range_maximum\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_minimum\": 9999999, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": 0.001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600\", \"indicating_range_maximum\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_minimum\": 9999999, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": 0.01}\n  ]\n}\n\nTable 10 (reduced bore, battery/renewable):\nrows:\nDN40, DN50: 9999999, 99999, 0.0001\nDN65: 9999999, 99999, 0.001\nDN80, DN100, DN125, DN150: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\nDN200: 9999999, 999999, 0.01\nDN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\nDN500, DN600: 9999999, 9999999, 0.1\n\nTable 11 (full bore, AC mains) merged with page 12 continuation:\nDN40, DN50: 9999999, 99999, 0.0001\nDN65: 9999999, 999999, 0.0001\nDN80, DN100, DN125, DN150: 9999999, 999999, 0.001\nDN200, DN250, DN300: 9999999, 9999999, 0.01\nDN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600: 